omx-panel (0.10.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A declared panel can show a control only while another control's value
    meets a rule (visibleWhen: a set of values, or a count reached). A hidden
    control takes no slot on a page, a section left empty has no page, and the
    MOD GUI shows and hides the control as the governing port moves (#123).
  * omx-panel modgui --films-only writes the film strips into a built bundle
    and touches nothing else, so a plugin tree need not track them.
  * A C renderer that draws a panel description into a CPU pixel buffer, RGBA
    or BGRA, at any size and scale, and a window for it through pugl and
    NanoVG; a control hidden by another control's value is not drawn (#120,
    #124). It is built and checked in CI; nothing of it is packaged yet.
  * The family role table ships as browser data,
    @openmixer/omx-panel/role-table; the copies check is exported as
    @openmixer/omx-panel/copies-check.
  * The tests read the example descriptors from @openmixer/omx-contract and
    keep no copy; the lilv proofs run in CI. The MOD GUI's modgui:javascript
    term is one sord_validate reads.
  * The package installs its licence and a short README and no other
    markdown; its description points to openmixer.org. The RPM asks for no
    development package at run time.
  * Every dependency on a sibling states a floor and a ceiling: omx-contract-data
    >= 3.6.0 and < 4, plugin-hostd-contract >= 0.18.0 and < 0.19, and
    omx-plugins-contract (recommended) >= 0.15.0 and < 0.20.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100

